## Why This Is Asked
Assess CSS architecture for responsive grid and nested components, accessibility, and performance without JS.

## Key Concepts
- CSS Grid and Flexbox interplay with responsive breakpoints
- aspect-ratio for chart area
- CSS custom properties for density toggles
- CSS-only accordion using inputs and sibling selectors
- staggered entrances with nth-child delays
- prefers-reduced-motion and focus-visible behavior

## Code Example
```css
:root { --pad: 16px; --gap: 16px; --title: 16px; }
[data-density="compact"] { --pad: 8px; --gap: 8px; --title: 14px; }
.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: var(--gap); }
.chart { aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; background: #e8eefc; }
.widget { padding: var(--pad); border-radius: 8px; background: #fff; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0,0,0,.08); }
@media (max-width: 1024px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
@media (max-width: 768px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); } }

.widget [type="checkbox"] { display:none; }
.panel { max-height: 0; overflow: hidden; transition: max-height .3s ease; }
.widget [type="checkbox"]:checked ~ .panel { max-height: 200px; }

@keyframes enter { from { transform: translateY(8px); opacity: 0; } to { transform: translateY(0); opacity: 1; } }
.grid .widget { animation: enter .4s var(--delay, 0s) forwards; }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .grid .widget { animation: none; } }
```

